Best Practice for Your Repository Platform

I would create a Document Generation Service with this flow:

Repository
      |
      v
Static Analysis
      |
      v
Repository Model
      |
      v
Bedrock JSON Response
      |
      v
Response Validator
(Pydantic)
      |
      v
Document Generator
      |
      +--> DOCX
      +--> PDF
      +--> HTML
      +--> Markdown
      +--> Confluence

The most important design decision is:

Never let Bedrock generate the final document format.

Instead:

Bedrock generates structured JSON.
Your application validates it.
Templates generate the professional documents.

This gives consistent formatting, version control, repeatable output, easier testing, and much higher-quality enterprise documentation.
